HOW TO READ THE ROWS BELOW
--------------------------

Each FILE row is one adapted file. `copy` is the verbatim upstream file, kept with a .txt suffix so
neither TypeScript nor Vite ever compiles it; `sha256` is that copy's hash, and it is the hash of the
upstream file at the commit above. Diff `copy` against the local file to see every change. The
general rules, which apply to every row:

  * Exports, prop types and state logic are upstream's. Import specifiers are swapped for the local
    stand-ins listed in the row, and BEM classes (`ai-<component>__<part>`) are appended beside the
    upstream Tailwind class strings, which are kept for traceability and are inert (this app has no
    Tailwind). The BEM classes are styled with the app's tokens in the component's .css file.
  * React 18: primitives that receive a ref through `asChild` or directly use forwardRef.
  * Anything beyond that is named in the row.

The local stand-ins, which have no upstream file of their own:

  lib/utils.ts            cn (clsx semantics; no tailwind-merge — there is no Tailwind to merge)
  lib/cva.ts              class-variance-authority's cva / VariantProps
  lib/floating.ts         viewport placement for portalled tooltip and listbox panels
  lib/use-isomorphic-layout-effect.ts
  ui/slot.tsx             radix-ui Slot (asChild), with composed refs
  icons.tsx               the lucide-react icons used, as inline SVG under the same names
                          (the ones added for chain-of-thought, tool, task, sources and
                          Reasoning's Brain take lucide-react 1.31.0's own icon geometry)
  stick-to-bottom.tsx     use-stick-to-bottom (StickToBottom, StickToBottom.Content,
                          useStickToBottomContext); "at the bottom" is lib/follow-latest.ts
  streamdown.tsx          streamdown + @streamdown/{cjk,code,math,mermaid}; renders through the
                          app's lib/markdown.tsx (marked + DOMPurify, fences to the code block)
  highlight-compat.ts     the shiki types and tokenizer CodeBlock uses, over lib/highlight.ts,
                          plus shiki's `diff` language (a line's colour from its first character)
  ai-types.ts             the `ai` package types the components name (type-only upstream)
  reasoning-compat.tsx    @radix-ui/react-use-controllable-state (Reasoning, ChainOfThought)
  lib/nanoid.ts           nanoid (a 21-character URL-safe id from crypto.getRandomValues)
  ui/dropdown-menu-primitive.tsx
                          radix-ui's DropdownMenu primitive, which ui/dropdown-menu.tsx
                          imports as a namespace (see that row)
  lib/cmdk.tsx            cmdk's Command, Input, List, Empty, Group, Item and Separator (a
                          substring filter where cmdk ranks fuzzily; no Command.Dialog)

The composer rows (prompt-input.tsx, attachments.tsx and the ui/ primitives added with them:
input-group, input, textarea, spinner, hover-card, dropdown-menu, command, dialog) were added on
2026-09-22. Their icons (CornerDownLeft, ArrowUp, Image, Monitor, Plus, Square, X, FileText, Globe,
Music2, Paperclip, Video, Loader2) are in icons.tsx with lucide-react 1.31.0's geometry, and an icon
is now aria-hidden unless it is given an aria-*, role or title prop — lucide's own rule, which the
Spinner (role="status", named "Loading") depends on.


