FILE prompt-input.tsx
  upstream: packages/elements/src/prompt-input.tsx
  copy: upstream/prompt-input.tsx.txt
  sha256: cf43baf5baa444b4ae06d250643b3fb2efd329c85f9b31a43e3aaf481dd27305
  substitutions:
    @repo/shadcn-ui/components/ui/command -> ./ui/command
    @repo/shadcn-ui/components/ui/dropdown-menu -> ./ui/dropdown-menu
    @repo/shadcn-ui/components/ui/hover-card -> ./ui/hover-card
    @repo/shadcn-ui/components/ui/input-group -> ./ui/input-group
    @repo/shadcn-ui/components/ui/select -> ./ui/select
    @repo/shadcn-ui/components/ui/spinner -> ./ui/spinner
    @repo/shadcn-ui/components/ui/tooltip -> ./ui/tooltip
    @repo/shadcn-ui/lib/utils -> ./lib/utils
    ai -> ./ai-types (type-only: ChatStatus, FileUIPart, SourceDocumentUIPart)
    lucide-react -> ./icons (CornerDownLeftIcon, ImageIcon, Monitor, PlusIcon, SquareIcon, XIcon)
    nanoid -> ./lib/nanoid
    styles -> ./prompt-input.css; the hidden file input keeps upstream's `hidden` class and adds
      `ai-prompt-input__file`, which that sheet hides (the app has no `.hidden` utility)
    SEND KEY: PromptInputTextarea hard-codes Enter-to-submit (`e.key === "Enter"` and not Shift).
      It takes `submitBinding` instead — a lib/shortcuts `Shortcut`, default lib/send-key
      ENTER_SEND, which is upstream's behaviour — matched with the app's shared `matchesShortcut`
      (../../lib/shortcuts), so the composer passes the person's `prefs.sendKey` binding and a
      "⌘Enter sends" choice makes a bare Enter a new line here. The IME (isComposing) guard and the
      disabled-submit check are upstream's. With the default binding a bare Enter with ⌘ or Ctrl
      held no longer submits (the shared matcher is exact about modifiers).
    FILES: `onAddFiles?: (files: File[]) => void` is added to PromptInputProps. When it is given,
      every file the picker, a paste or a drop yields is handed to it as it arrived: no
      accept / maxFileSize / maxFiles filter here, no blob: URL, nothing kept in the local
      attachment list, and the submit passes `files: []` without running the blob-to-data-URL
      conversion. The composer uploads each file as it is staged (lib/api.ts uploadAttachment,
      with progress, abort and retry) and applies its own admission rules (lib/attachments.ts), so a
      refused file gets the same sentence however it arrived. `add` keeps one identity through a
      ref, so the drop listeners are not re-attached each render. Without `onAddFiles`, upstream's
      model is unchanged. Backspace-in-an-empty-box removes the last attachment in upstream's list,
      which is empty in that mode, so it does nothing there.
    REFUSAL: onSubmit's type widens to `void | boolean | Promise<void | boolean>`, and a `false`
      result (or a promise resolving to it) is a refusal: the form is not reset and neither the
      attachments nor the referenced sources are cleared, as with a throw. Upstream reset the form
      BEFORE the result was known; the reset now runs only after an accepted result. (Upstream's
      comment gives the reason it ran first: text typed during an asynchronous blob conversion. That
      conversion never runs for a caller with `onAddFiles`, and the composer's textarea is
      controlled, so its reset changes nothing.)
    REACT 18: PromptInputTextarea and PromptInputButton are forwardRef components (their prop types
      keep upstream's names); PromptInputActionMenuTrigger and tooltips reach the button through
      `asChild`, and the composer measures and focuses its textarea through the ref.
    PromptInputSubmit keeps upstream's "Stop" / "Submit" names, which its props override; the
      composer passes "Stop this run" and "Send".
END

